        article("micron::posix::unix_address", "linux/sys/unix_socket.hpp", "Fixed Linux Unix-domain address with family 1 and a 108-byte path array.", [
            "unix_stream_socket returns a close-on-exec fd_t value; it does not add a socket-owning destructor. unix_connect checks only that the supplied address length is between three and sizeof(unix_address), then delegates to the kernel. The path buffer and explicit length determine pathname/abstract-address encoding."
        ]),
        article("micron::posix::utsname_t", "linux/sys/system.hpp", "Six fixed 65-byte arrays filled by uname: system, node, release, version, machine, and domain names.", [
            "The record owns its character arrays and has no dynamic allocation. uname returns raw status; no automatic query occurs merely by declaring the record. System identity strings are descriptive data and are not capability probes for newer operations."
        ]),
        article("micron::host_dso", "linux/dynamic.hpp", "Borrowed view of an already discovered host ELF module.", [
            "Construction finds an existing host module by soname and throws if absent. The default is empty. sym resolves a defined symbol through the module's dynamic metadata; sym_as casts the result without checking a callable signature. Copies do not pin or retain a host mapping. The registry metadata and module code/data must remain alive for every retained pointer, path, or soname view."
        ]),
        article("micron::dso", "linux/dynamic.hpp", "Move-only owning native ELF handle with soname or explicit-path construction.", [
            "Each instance owns an independent mapping through elf::handle_t; it does not deduplicate or share dlopen-style references. Destruction releases the handle, and moving transfers it. Symbol pointers are borrowed from that mapping and expire on destruction/replacement. Use host_dso to inspect a module already owned by the host, and the dynamic module registry when its explicit reference/dependency protocol is required."
        ]),
        article("micron::sysctl_toplevel", "linux/sysctl.hpp", "Legacy numeric sysctl selector vocabulary without an access implementation.", [
            "The enum families describe kernel/VM/network/filesystem/device/bus/ABI selectors, with nested protocol/configuration/cache/driver-specific numbers. Their numeric presence does not establish a current kernel node or deprecated syscall's availability. No function in this header maps these selectors to a path or reads/writes /proc/sys. Use explicit node paths with sysfs readers when that is the intended operation."
        ], ["micron::sysctl_" + name for name in "bus inotify kern vm net random pty busisa netcore netunix netfilter netipv4 netipv4route netipv4conf netipv4netfilter netipv6 netipv6route netipv6conf netipv6icmp netneigh netdccp netipx netllc netllc2timeout netatalk netnetrom netax25 netrose netx25 nettr netdecnet netdecnetconfdev netsctp netbridge fs fsquota dev devcdrom devraid devparportdefault devparport devmachid devscsi devipmi abi".split()]),
